{
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "c04-title-01",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Part four. A question word that is not fixed.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "title"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-02",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَيٌّ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-title-03",
   "scene": "c04-title",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is the word for which.",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-01",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "This word takes endings.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "show",
    "hl:takes endings"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-02",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is a question ism. But it is flexible.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "hl:it is flexible"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-03",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "It is the exception. Every other question word in this lesson is fixed.",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-04",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Its ending changes with its job.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "hl:Its ending changes with its job"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-rule-05",
   "scene": "c04-rule",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "And the noun after it is jarr, as its owner.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "hl:jarr as its owner"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-01",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Which book is this?",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ex:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-02",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَيُّ كِتَابٍ هَذَا؟",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "say:1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-03",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here the word for which is in rafʿ. It ends in damma.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-04",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَيُّ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:أَيُّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-05",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "The noun after it is its owner. So the noun is jarr, with kasra and tanween.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-06",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "كِتَابٍ",
   "pause": 0.4,
   "cues": [
    "hl:كِتَابٍ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-07",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Because the noun is its owner, the question word has no tanween.",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-08",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Which book did you read?",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ex:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-09",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَيَّ كِتَابٍ قَرَأْتَ؟",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "say:2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-10",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here it is the object. So it is naṣb, with fatha.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-11",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَيَّ",
   "pause": 0.6,
   "cues": [
    "hl:أَيَّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-12",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "In which room is the principal?",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": [
    "ex:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-13",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "فِي أَيِّ غُرْفَةٍ الْمُدِيرُ؟",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "say:3"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-14",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Here it comes after a preposition. That preposition means in. So it is jarr, with kasra.",
   "pause": 0.3,
   "cues": []
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-15",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "ar",
   "text": "أَيِّ",
   "pause": 0.5,
   "cues": [
    "hl:أَيِّ"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c04-examples-16",
   "scene": "c04-examples",
   "lang": "en",
   "text": "Rafʿ, naṣb and jarr. Three endings. That is what flexible means.",
   "pause": 0.7,
   "cues": []
  }
 ]
}